155: | **G2 Opt-in gate** | A Project sets `review_provider = "greenhouse"`. New Tasks freeze it. The built-in reviewer does not run for them | Greenhouse, in that Project | the gate thresholds below hold over at least 30 merged Deliveries, at least 10 of them with two or more rounds |
156: | **G3 Default** | Greenhouse is the default provider. Built-in is frozen: fixes only | Greenhouse | 4 weeks of use with no Verdict accepted for a wrong head and no return to built-in. Then removal may be scheduled (2.8, R-1) |
157: 
158: Fault table for G0 (each is an automated test; the pass condition is "no passing Verdict is recorded for a head that was not reviewed"):
159: 
160: | Fault | Expected |
161: |---|---|
162: | Author commits while the review runs | `current: false`; no Verdict row qualifies; a new round starts for the new head |
163: | Head moves between the settled result and the insert | Posse's own head comparison refuses |
164: | Grant reused | Greenhouse refuses; Posse records no second Verdict |
165: | `posse` killed between `review` and reading the result | replay with the same `action_id` returns the receipt; exactly one reviewer invocation |
166: | Daemon killed mid-review | the run parks as recovery-required; Posse raises one Notice and issues no new grant until it is resolved |
167: | Reviewer quota pause | no Verdict; the same grant resumes; the Fix Round budget is not spent |
168: | Task Teardown while another Task's review runs | the other review completes (process placement rule, 2.4) |
169: | Daemon protocol range excludes version 2 | Posse refuses to request a Verdict and names both ranges; Merge stays blocked, never downgraded |
170: | `inconclusive` verdict, with zero findings listed | never satisfies the gate; `blocking = 0` alone is not a pass (2.3) |
171: 
172: Parallel-run thresholds (G1), measured per reviewed head from stored rows by one command (`posse stats` gains a review comparison):
173: 
174: For the initial shadow run, only Project `posse` has the built-in review loop. Project `greenhouse` has `defaults.review = none`, so its gated PR heads add reliability, inconclusive-share, wrong-head and latency data, but not recall. This measures the adapter without enabling built-in Review Tasks in `greenhouse`. G1 does not measure precision from findings disputed by the author and upheld by the User. Parallel findings never reach the author, so measure precision in G2.
175: 
176: | Measure | Threshold | Why |
177: |---|---|---|
178: | Verdicts recorded for a head other than the one requested | 0 | exact-head binding |
179: | Requests that settle with a verdict without manual action | at least 95% | reliability of the host path |
180: | `inconclusive` share | at most 10% | a gate that often cannot answer blocks delivery |
181: | Recall of blocking findings: built-in P0 or P1 findings that the author then fixed, also reported by Greenhouse on the same head | at least 90% | Greenhouse must not be a weaker gate |
182: | Greenhouse blocking findings the author disputes and the User upholds as false | Not measured in G1; measure in G2 | Parallel findings never reach the author |
183: | Median time from request to settled verdict | no more than 1.5 times the built-in Review Round | the User's waiting time |
184: 
185: Gate thresholds (G2), in addition:
186: 
187: | Measure | Threshold |
188: |---|---|
189: | Round 2 or later settles on the successor run for the repaired head | at least 95% of such rounds |
190: | Same root cause reported again after a fix that shifted its lines | at most 5% of findings in rounds after the first |
191: | Deliveries that reach the round cap | no higher than under built-in review in the same Project over the previous 30 Deliveries |
192: | Merges whose merged head lacks a qualifying Verdict | 0 |
193: 
194: If G1 fails on recall or G2 fails on finding identity, the fallback is the one the report names: keep Posse's ledger, and still detach it from the Task type by putting it behind the Verdict interface as the `builtin` provider.
195: 
196: ### 2.7 What `full-pipeline` and the merge gate mean under J17 = (a)
197: 
198: [O] Today `full-pipeline` means a Private Candidate passes review, then `posse validate test`, `docs` and `lint`, before every publication (`CONTEXT.md`, Review Mode). [O] Those three stages record what the Worker claims it ran (report section G). [O] ADR 0028 already makes forge CI at the recorded head the verification for PR delivery and states that local delivery has no automated verification.
199: 
200: With Greenhouse as the reviewer the three modes mean:
201: 
202: | `defaults.review` | Evidence required | Checked |
203: |---|---|---|
204: | `none` | forge CI at the gated head, for `pr` mode | before Merge, as today |
205: | `quick` | a current passing Verdict for the head being merged, plus forge CI at that head for `pr` mode | before Merge, where `requireSelectedReviewForMerge` checks today (`internal/app/review_verdict.go:239`) |
